0; all false discovery rate values <0.001). Tumor-purity adjustment attenuated but did not eliminate most associations with LM22 immune-cell and immune-checkpoint signatures. Coexpressed transcripts were enriched in regulated exocytosis, calcium-dependent exocytosis, dense-core granule exocytosis, and vesicle-related processes. No integrated cancer hallmark reached significance after multiple-testing correction. C4orf50 is overexpressed in breast cancer and its continuous expression is associated with overall survival and immune-related transcriptional features in TCGA-BRCA. These observational findings do not establish a causal role for C4orf50 and require validation in independent cohorts and experimental models.",
