"source": "journal",
"server": null,
"pmid": "42201779",
"doi": "10.1158/1078-0432.ccr-25-1629",
"title": "HRDetect in Tubo-ovarian Carcinoma: Stratification and Therapeutic Implications",
"authors": [
"Banda K",
"Davies HR",
"Kumar Y",
"Memari Y",
"Degasperi A",
"Radke M",
"Rodriguez I",
"Gooley TA",
"Katz R",
"Menghi F",
"Harding T",
"Lin K",
"Liu ET",
"Nik-Zainal S",
"Swisher EM"
],
"author_string": "Banda K, Davies HR, Kumar Y, Memari Y, Degasperi A, Radke M, Rodriguez I, Gooley TA, Katz R, Menghi F, Harding T, Lin K, Liu ET, Nik-Zainal S, Swisher EM.",
"journal": "Clinical cancer research : an official journal of the American Association for Cancer Research",
"year": 2026,
"date": "2026-09-01",
"field": "cancergen",
"sections": [
{
"label": "Purpose",
"text": "To evaluate HRDetect, a mutational signature-based algorithm, for prognostic utility in tubo-ovarian carcinoma and to determine if whole-genome sequencing (WGS) with rearrangement signature (RS) analysis can refine genomic classification beyond the traditional homologous recombination-deficient versus homologous recombination-proficient framework."
},
{
"label": "Experimental design",
"text": "WGS was performed on matched tumor-normal pairs from 185 patients with advanced-stage tubo-ovarian carcinoma from the University of Washington (UW) cohort. HRDetect scores were calculated using substitution signatures, RS, microhomology-mediated deletions, and global loss of heterozygosity. An independent validation cohort (ARIEL2, n = 77) of platinum-sensitive tubo-ovarian carcinoma treated with rucaparib was analyzed to correlate HRDetect with PARP inhibitor (PARPi) response. RS analysis and unsupervised hierarchical clustering were employed to delineate genomic subgroups."
},
{
"label": "Results",
"text": "In the UW cohort, 51.4% of cases were classified as HRDetect-high and had significantly prolonged median overall survival versus others [6.2 vs. 4.1 years; hazard ratio (HR), 0.6; 95% confidence interval (CI), 0.41-0.87; P = 0.007]. Furthermore, 48.4% of HRDetect-high tumors harbored BRCA1/2 mutations or BRCA1 promoter methylation, whereas 22.1% lacked BRCA1/2 alterations. A substantial fraction (23.2%) fell into an HRDetect-intermediate category, highlighting greater genomic heterogeneity than currently appreciated. RS profiling uncovered 11 genomic clusters, with specific RS profiles (RS1, RS14, and RS18) correlating with poor survival. In ARIEL2, HRDetect-high tumors showed better PARPi responses, with improved progression-free survival (11.1 vs. 7.1 months; HR, 0.44; 95% CI, 0.26-0.74; P = 0.03) and response rates (54% vs. 22.5%)."
},
{
"label": "Conclusions",
"text": "HRDetect predicts survival and sensitivity to PARPi in tubo-ovarian carcinoma. Combined with RS-based clustering, it reveals unappreciated genomic heterogeneity and supports a nuanced stratification framework to improve precision oncology in tubo-ovarian carcinoma."
}
],
"n_chars": 2044,
"structured": true,
"has_results": true,
