"doi": "10.1016/j.bioactmat.2026.09.043",
"title": "DNA-adsorbing nanozyme hydrogel reprograms the immuno-oxidative microenvironment to support stem cell-based cartilage repair in osteoarthritis",
"authors": [
"Yu H",
"Hu Z",
"Tan Q",
"Wang C",
"Wang B",
"Yan Y",
"Yu Y",
"Zhang F",
"Zhang M",
"Huang Y",
"Cai D",
"Wang Y",
"Zhou H",
"Wang D",
"Cheng W"
],
"author_string": "Yu H, Hu Z, Tan Q, Wang C, Wang B, Yan Y, Yu Y, Zhang F, Zhang M, Huang Y, Cai D, Wang Y, Zhou H, Wang D, Cheng W.",
"journal": "Bioactive materials",
"year": 2027,
"date": "2026-10-11",
"field": "cfdna",
"sections": [
{
"label": null,
"text": "Osteoarthritis (OA) is a prevalent degenerative joint disease, and stem cell therapy is often limited by a hostile joint microenvironment. Excessive reactive oxygen species (ROS) and damage-associated cell-free DNA (cfDNA) cooperatively drive innate immune activation, inflammatory macrophage polarization, and chondrogenic instability, forming an immuno-oxidative barrier to cartilage repair. Here, we developed a bioactive DNA-adsorbing nanozyme hydrogel (MNKB/HA) to remodel this niche and enhance BMSC-mediated cartilage repair. MNKB/HA integrates Mn 3 O 4 nanozymes with Kartogenin (KGN)-engineered bone marrow mesenchymal stem cells (BMSCs) in an injectable hyaluronic acid matrix. Mn 3 O 4 exhibited SOD- and CAT-like activities, scavenging O 2 · - , H 2 O 2 , and ·OH, while efficiently adsorbing cfDNA and CpG-ODN to suppress TLR9/MyD88 signaling and M1 polarization and promote M2 polarization. In vitro, 10 μg/mL Mn 3 O 4 was cytocompatible, protected BMSCs and chondrocytes from H 2 O 2 -induced apoptosis, and reshaped inflammatory secretion, with IL-10 increased 8.3-fold and TNF-α, IL-6, and IL-1β reduced. KGN stabilized the chondrogenic phenotype (SOX9, COL Ⅱ, ACAN), while its combination with Mn 3 O 4 synergistically enhanced chondrogenic stability under oxidative/inflammatory stress. In rat OA, intra-articular MNKB/HA reduced OARSI scores, restored COL II and ACAN, decreased MMP13, improved subchondral bone microarchitecture, and attenuated synovitis and osteophytes. MNKB/HA also reduced synovial cfDNA, weakened TLR9 signaling, promoted M2 polarization, and showed intra-articular retention for at least 10 days without notable systemic toxicity. Thus, MNKB/HA remodels the immuno-oxidative niche through synergistic ROS scavenging and cfDNA adsorption, providing a strategy for stem cell-mediated cartilage repair in OA."
}
],
