"pmid": "40248734",
"doi": "10.21037/tlcr-24-800",
"title": "<i>ANKRD11</i> as a potential biomarker for brain metastasis from lung adenocarcinoma via cerebrospinal fluid liquid biopsy",
"authors": [
"Sun Q",
"Xing P",
"Wang Q",
"Xia Z",
"Li J",
"Li Z",
"Meng F",
"Liu T",
"Wang S",
"Yin R"
],
"author_string": "Sun Q, Xing P, Wang Q, Xia Z, Li J, Li Z, Meng F, Liu T, Wang S, Yin R.",
"journal": "Translational lung cancer research",
"year": 2025,
"date": "2025-03-03",
"field": "cfdna",
"sections": [
{
"label": "Background",
"text": "Brain metastasis (BM) explains the majority of lung cancer-related mortality, especially lung adenocarcinoma (LUAD). The extensive clinical adoption of liquid biopsy presents a minimally invasive approach for the early detection and treatment management of brain metastasis from lung adenocarcinoma (BM-LUAD). Nonetheless, biomarkers for assessing BM-LUAD remain insufficient. This study aims to reveal novel biomarkers for BM-LUAD through the liquid biopsy of cerebrospinal fluid (CSF)."
},
{
"label": "Methods",
"text": "Circulating tumor DNA (ctDNA)-based panel sequencing was conducted on CSF samples from seven patients with BM-LUAD. Additionally, single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) data from normal lung tissue, primary tumors, and BMs were analyzed using publicly available datasets. Functional assays were performed on cell lines, complemented by in vivo studies in nude mice."
},
{
"label": "Results",
"text": "CSF liquid biopsy identified high-frequency mutations in EGFR, BRCA2 , and ANKRD11 among patients with BM-LUAD. Further analysis highlighted ANKRD11 as a potential biomarker, showing reduced expression in tumor tissues and significant prognostic implications. ScRNA-seq revealed a progressive decrease in ANKRD11 expression along tumor progression, while in vitro and in vivo assays confirmed its role in suppressing tumor invasion and metastasis."
},
{
"label": "Conclusions",
"text": "Our study highlights the potential of ctDNA-based CSF liquid biopsy in identifying BM-LUAD, and the efficacy in revealing novel biomarkers for BM-LUAD. Data analyses and functional assays indicated ANKRD11 as a predictive biomarker for BM-LUAD. This result addresses, to some extent, the existing gap in biomarkers for BM-LUAD."
}
],
"n_chars": 1629,
